WEBVTT

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:45.040
<i>Beneath the softly setting sun</i>

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:49.950
<i>where the shadows grow long</i>

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:55.920
<i>pointing the way as the rain sings its song.</i>

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:01.730
<i>We'll look for a rainbow,</i>

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.120
<i>then we'll roam back,</i>

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:13.530
<i>by the cool of the night sky,</i>

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:18.950
<i>as the stars guide us home.</i>

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:24.980
<i>That familiar, bright moon,
the soft beam it will give</i>

00:02:24.980 --> 00:02:33.490
<i>like an old friend now leading
us back to where we live.</i>

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.590
That song, what is it?

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:39.250
It's popular.

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:41.600
Oh, it sounds like an oldie.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.800
Doesn't it? But I like it.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:48.500
Well, I think that should keep the rain out.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.610
Oh, the storage room light isn't working.

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:53.620
Could you take a look at it later?

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:55.820
And the lawn mower, too...

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.950
Hey, keeping me busy, huh?

00:02:58.250 --> 00:02:59.400
Sorry.

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:02.020
It's fine. It has been three months.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:41.320
You can't look at the night sky?

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:52.510
I start thinking...

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:55.750
"What if something happened
to you in that sea of stars?"

00:03:55.750 --> 00:03:56.880
Don't worry.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:58.460
After this mission...

00:03:58.460 --> 00:03:59.600
Liar.

00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:03.280
There will be others after this one.

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:08.120
You've said that for six years and I believed you.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:09.720
Kroka...

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.810
Sometimes, I tell myself...

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:20.600
that when you're home, you're just a dream.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.780
One that comes back every
few months or years...

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:26.470
An impossible dream...

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:41.970
I'm not a dream.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:44.090
You might as well be to me.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:47.350
All you are is a ring...

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.660
You only say that you're more.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.130
Enough!

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:59.130
You've never understood how I felt at all!

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:02.450
If that's so, I would have
thought of you as a dream, too.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:07.240
A dream I only have when I'm back on Earth!

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:11.980
A dream...

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:15.580
As King John said...

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:19.850
"With my words of challenge,
you shall come home safely".

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:24.720
You're the flash of light that shoots
through the king of France's eye.

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:27.800
Let's shoot them.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.540
The eyes of lazy high officials

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:33.770
and everyone else who doesn't
know how to dream anymore.

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:37.300
Enjoy the taste of Earth.

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:07.200
Is it real?

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:10.550
We've extrapolated the
data from the Odysseus...

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:12.940
and the probability is 60%.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.110
It's possible it could be a Penrose Twister Hole.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:23.480
Colonel Lawrence, telephone.

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:28.090
No, however...

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.540
Nonsense, it's impossible now!

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:33.670
But...

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:35.000
Yes.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.070
No...

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:43.870
Understood...

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:48.020
Colonel?

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:51.470
The Odysseus will explore
the special gravitational point.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:52.890
That can't be!

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.380
If they use Neptune's gravity,
they can do a fly-by.

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:57.440
That's crazy!

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:01.090
They'll miss a chance to
dock with the supply tanker!

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:05.760
The Office of Development only
wants to secure next year's budget!

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:07.200
And for that reason...

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:08.620
I know!

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.300
But I'm asking you, please.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.630
Change directions now?

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:17.110
That's impossible!

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:20.070
At worst, we'll be space castaways.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:21.950
But the calculations...

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:26.740
...could also mean finding
a window into hyperspace.

00:07:26.990 --> 00:07:29.860
Or even a chance of interplanetary travel.

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:30.850
But...

00:07:31.030 --> 00:07:32.960
We're all in a tough spot.

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:36.960
We've been wishing for a breakthrough.

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:39.660
The space program has been stalled.

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:43.230
We have no new discoveries or even surprises...

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:46.040
Isn't that right, Lawrence?

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:50.940
"Great acts of heroism
are often soon forgotten."

00:07:51.710 --> 00:07:55.770
"But the glory of the deed
itself...that will never die."

00:07:56.720 --> 00:07:59.880
"Perseverance keeps honor bright."

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:04.260
"For honor travels in a strait so
narrow where one but goes abreast."

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.420
What is that?

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.730
Lines spoken by Ulysses...

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.790
...from "Troilus and Cressida" by Shakespeare.

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:12.300
He says it often.

00:08:22.810 --> 00:08:23.800
Let's go.

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:26.110
For those who will come after us.

00:08:27.050 --> 00:08:31.110
And to play the flash of light that
will shoot through people's eyes.

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:41.620
But I forgot about it somehow.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:45.390
Or maybe I didn't let
myself think about it.

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.440
About those who disappeared
into the darkness...

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:51.630
...behind the success and glory.

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:14.420
Is that...

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.520
...a star?

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:16.790
No, it's not.

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:32.450
Wh-What is this place?

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:40.020
I-It's so beautiful.

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:46.620
Like the light of a fairy.

00:09:56.370 --> 00:10:01.040
I wish I could show you
this beautiful world, too...

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:04.970
If that's so, I would've
thought of you as a dream, too.

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:08.380
Kroka...

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:10.340
I'm sorry...

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:12.010
I'm sorry.

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:15.320
You aren't a dream.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:17.660
I want to see you one last time, and...

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:22.420
The next time I regained consciousness,

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:25.100
it was in front of my eyes.

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:28.260
The familiar shape of the Earth was there.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.100
Just to go home...

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:35.090
Just to travel between planets...

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:38.350
I sacrificed my own feelings

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:41.550
just so I could return to that blue planet.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:42.810
It can't be...

00:10:43.020 --> 00:10:44.990
And if it is true...

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:46.550
No way...

00:10:46.750 --> 00:10:49.380
You're saying the alien isn't an alien?

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:51.560
What's the matter, Sue?

00:10:52.050 --> 00:10:55.260
Frank is remembering things
that happened before, right?

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:58.980
He'll tell us about the land
he was born in, right?

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:08.930
Commander.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:10.370
I heard it all.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:13.170
But should we believe it?

00:11:15.050 --> 00:11:16.120
This means he...

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:18.050
Or should I say "they"...

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:20.490
...are not visitors after all.

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:22.490
They've sacrificed themselves...

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:24.260
Been through different bodies...

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:25.780
Just so they could return.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:31.960
Commander...

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:35.270
If it's true,

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:39.000
why have we been fighting up
until now and for what reason?

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:41.170
Tell me, Guenevere.

00:11:42.680 --> 00:11:46.840
Early warning systems detect
new intruders inside lunar orbit.

00:11:47.180 --> 00:11:48.520
27 in all.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:49.750
They're aliens.

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:53.480
All descending toward Pilgrimage Point.

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:03.090
Understood.

00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:04.820
Fine.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.100
We have orders.

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:14.010
We'll let all the aliens head to Pilgrimage Point.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:15.270
The army won't resist.

00:12:15.340 --> 00:12:16.780
That can't be!

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.330
Everyone knows.

00:12:18.610 --> 00:12:22.320
The catastrophe caused by
reaching Pilgrimage Point...

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:23.980
...was just a fabrication.

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:25.240
Then...

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:27.680
A massive thermonuclear response.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.270
Frank!

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:56.540
Hey, so is your real name "Yuri"?

00:13:00.820 --> 00:13:04.350
What should I call you from now on?

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:05.780
Mr. Fairy?

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:07.050
Frank?

00:13:07.400 --> 00:13:08.560
Or Yuri?

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:12.430
Thank you.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.360
For singing.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:19.200
And for that beautiful ring of flowers.

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:33.350
At that moment, I was convinced
that despite my lack of memory,

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:35.960
Even though my form had changed,

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.960
I was not a dream or anything else.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.430
Of course not!

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:44.790
Because you saved me time
after time, didn't you, Frank?

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:46.030
Right?

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:48.700
And in the sea of my consciousness,

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.700
there was a woman who questioned my identity.

00:13:55.340 --> 00:13:58.340
I wanted to save her.

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:01.180
You can't mean...

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:02.170
Maki...

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:08.790
Please tell me!

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:11.050
What did Maki leave you?

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:14.830
Who's Maki?

00:14:15.460 --> 00:14:16.590
Maki Agata.

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:20.100
Dr. Noguchi's assistant who helped build Frank.

00:14:31.110 --> 00:14:32.290
Commander?

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:45.020
What brings you here?

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:47.660
I wanted to see it with my own eyes.

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:53.960
This is Pilgrimage Point.

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:01.480
I've only seen pictures.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:06.440
But soon, this place will no longer exist...

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:12.850
There's a problem.

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:13.990
What is it?

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:15.220
He's still...

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:16.210
Frank's...

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:18.460
What's wrong?

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:20.620
Please answer me.

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:22.340
I'll be waiting.

00:15:24.430 --> 00:15:26.160
This is goodbye, Hattie.

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:29.370
Wait!

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:30.360
Wait up!

00:15:30.360 --> 00:15:35.380
I have to apologize to my wife for
what I've done and said in the past.

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:39.540
We aren't dreams.

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:44.480
I'm the only one on the Earth.

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:48.740
Frank!

00:15:52.590 --> 00:15:53.820
We don't have time.

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:56.820
The aliens will be here in less than an hour.

00:15:57.870 --> 00:15:59.030
Bring him back.

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.490
We can't leave a comrade behind.

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:04.590
Ma'am!

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:25.090
I remember.

00:16:25.830 --> 00:16:29.260
Yes, it's all just as it was.

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:37.190
Wait!

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:38.880
Hey, wait!

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:40.770
Just over this hill...

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:51.810
Yes, that's right.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.980
The small path where I walked with her...

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:00.480
I've returned.

00:17:27.120 --> 00:17:28.890
Th-This is...

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:36.260
Kroka...

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:37.790
You...

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:49.080
Welcome home, Yuri Leonov.

00:17:49.740 --> 00:17:51.290
That voice...

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:54.250
It's been a long, long journey.

00:17:54.250 --> 00:17:55.780
David Lawrence.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:58.460
General Lawrence.

00:17:58.460 --> 00:17:59.420
General?

00:17:59.420 --> 00:18:00.850
Why are you...

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:03.550
You thought I was under house arrest, right?

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:09.160
When it's inconvenient, they
lock you away for a while.

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:11.930
An individual or group is no different.

00:18:12.970 --> 00:18:17.270
The first deep space explorer
vanished several decades ago.

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:20.140
That ship's captain has changed forms,

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:23.950
been through several torturous
trips, and yet headed home.

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:29.280
A grand voyage, bombarded
by heavy metals like asteroids.

00:18:29.420 --> 00:18:33.650
Is he man-made or a product of nature?

00:18:35.320 --> 00:18:38.590
A neutron in his brain
responded to an electric charge,

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:43.030
a thought process, then
started to form a specific figure.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:44.590
Impossible!

00:18:45.670 --> 00:18:47.660
How else can we explain this?

00:18:48.240 --> 00:18:50.810
Right, Mr. Ryu Soma?

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:53.940
Please tell me...

00:18:54.680 --> 00:18:56.540
Where is my wife?

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:20.960
What is that?

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:46.380
Darling, watch over me...

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:15.220
Let's go home...

00:20:24.470 --> 00:20:26.960
I only heard recently.

00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:43.210
Forgive me, Yuri.

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:47.920
If I hadn't asked you to
change course that day...

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:50.780
I was a fool.

00:20:52.190 --> 00:20:55.290
I forgot how much she meant to me.

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:57.650
Yuri?

00:20:57.650 --> 00:20:59.760
The hope of seeing her again...

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:03.160
This foolish path I've chosen...

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:05.570
It's ended everything.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:06.900
No.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:08.280
Yuri, you're...

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:11.800
I should never have come back here...

00:21:12.350 --> 00:21:14.710
What's the matter, Frank?

00:21:14.710 --> 00:21:16.420
I'm a fool!

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:32.290
There, too.

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:45.970
Frank...

00:21:48.980 --> 00:21:50.140
Yuri!

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:01.290
Frank...

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:02.420
He's crying.

00:22:04.030 --> 00:22:05.020
Yes.

00:22:05.100 --> 00:22:06.960
He's crying.

00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:39.030
It is hard to be true to yourself.

00:22:39.030 --> 00:22:42.340
But at the end of the game,
that is all there is.

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:44.460
A rhapsody of will in the distance.

00:22:45.410 --> 00:22:48.600
Next time,
Truth and Destruction.
